1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,940
1. Google sign-in uses OpenID to identify the account.
Google Calendar access is authorized separately.

2
00:00:11,940 --> 00:00:21,940
Moa Calendar: optional Google Calendar import.
This demo uses a previously authorized account.

3
00:00:21,940 --> 00:00:29,940
2. Re-authorize Google Calendar access for the demo.
The same OAuth client is used for sign-in and calendar import.

4
00:00:29,940 --> 00:00:51,940
Requested scope: calendar.events.readonly
Read-only event access; Google events are not modified.

5
00:00:51,940 --> 00:00:55,940
Google Calendar authorization is complete.
The app returns to the Moa calendar.

6
00:00:55,940 --> 00:01:05,940
3. Create the destination calendar: OAuth Review Demo.
This demo calendar has only one member.

7
00:01:05,940 --> 00:01:22,940
4. Select an import range and acknowledge sharing.
Imported titles, times and notes are visible to calendar members.

8
00:01:22,940 --> 00:01:36,940
5. Import succeeded: one event was copied from Google Calendar.
OAuth Demo Meeting appears in the destination calendar.

9
00:01:36,940 --> 00:01:51,940
The imported event shows its title, 21:30-22:30 KST time and description.
Moa reads these fields using events.list for the primary Google calendar.
